#: src/rules/sections.js:369
msgid "Is there check or checkmate?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:369
msgid "There is no check: you win by capturing the king. The nearest thing to checkmate is a king that cannot escape: the game ends at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:370
msgid "Why didn’t my piece move?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:370
msgid "The result was Missed. The piece wasn’t really on its square, its path was blocked, or your own piece was on the target. The board has updated to match what you learned."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:371
msgid "My rook is suddenly in two places, but I never split it!"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:371
msgid "It slid past a square where another piece might have been. Where that piece was in the way, the rook stayed; where it wasn’t, the rook arrived. Now the two pieces are linked."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:372
msgid "Can a ghost capture?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:372
msgid "Yes, but only if it is really there: a 50% part captures with a 50% chance. To capture for certain, merge its parts onto the target."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:373
msgid "Why can’t I split this piece?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:373
msgid "The tooltip tells you: it is a king or a pawn, a target is not empty for certain, no possibility has both paths clear, the piece would be on more than 4 squares, or your budget is full."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:376
msgid "Can I re-roll by undoing?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:377
msgid "No. In local games the same move in the same position always gets the same result."
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:384
msgid "The percentages say 67% and 33%. Why not halves?"
msgstr ""

#: src/rules/sections.js:385
msgid "After a roll, the remaining possibilities share the chance in proportion."
msgstr ""

