#: src/variants/makruk.js:367
msgid "The Khun (king) starts on d1 for White and on e8 for Black, with the Met beside it, and never castles; the Bia (pawns) start on each side's third rank."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:368
msgid "The Met steps one square diagonally, the Khon one square diagonally or straight forward, and the Ma, Rua and Khun move like the knight, rook and king."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:369
msgid "A Bia moves one square forward and captures one square diagonally forward; it never moves two squares (so there is no en passant), and on its sixth rank it always becomes a Met."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:370
msgid "Stalemate (not attacked, but every move would expose the Khun) is a draw, and if it is a stalemate in only some possibilities, a roll decides."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:371
msgid "When no Bia is left and one side has only its Khun, the other side must capture that Khun within a set number of its moves, counted from the lone Khun's first move after the last capture or promotion, or the game is drawn."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:372
msgid "That number is the first that applies of 8 (two Rua), 16 (one Rua), 22 (two Khon), 32 (two Ma), 44 (one Khon) and 64, minus the number of pieces on the board (both Khuns included), plus one, and at least one."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:373
msgid "When no Bia is left, the game is also drawn after 65 moves by each side without a capture or promotion, and it is drawn when only the two Khuns are left."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:374
msgid "These draws wait while the player to move can capture the enemy Khun for certain."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:434
msgid "a Khun was captured"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: Makruk: every move of the loser would have let its Khun (king) be captured for certain
#: src/variants/makruk.js:437
msgid "the Khun could not escape"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:441
msgid "only the two Khuns are left"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:443
msgid "the counting rule: the lone Khun was not captured in time"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:445
msgid "65 moves by each side since the last capture or promotion, with no Bia left"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:460
msgid "Counting: {done} of {allow} moves to capture the lone Khun"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/makruk.js:469
msgid "Moves without a capture: {n} of 65"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:141
msgid "Unicorn"
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:199
msgid "The board is a cube of five levels, from A at the bottom (White's home) to E at the top (Black's home); a cell is named level, file, rank, so Cc3 is the centre."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:203
msgid "Rooks move straight, also up and down; bishops move diagonally within any flat slice of the cube; unicorns move through the corners, changing level, file and rank at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:207
msgid "The queen moves like a rook, bishop or unicorn, the king steps to any of the 26 touching cells, and the knight jumps 2 cells one way and 1 another, also across levels."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:211
msgid "Pawns step one cell forward or one level up, and capture one cell forward and sideways, up and sideways, or forward and up, never straight ahead or straight up. For Black, forward is towards rank 1 and up is towards level A."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:215
msgid "A pawn that reaches the far rank of the opponent's home level (White: rank 5 of E; Black: rank 1 of A) must become a queen, rook, bishop, knight or unicorn."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:219
msgid "There is no castling, no double step and no en passant."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/raumschach.js:221
msgid "If only the two kings are left and they do not touch, the game is drawn."
msgstr ""

