#: src/variants/threecheck.js:256
msgid "Give check three times to win. Capturing the king also wins."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/threecheck.js:257
msgid "A check is a move after which one of your pieces (not your king) attacks the enemy king; a double check counts once."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/threecheck.js:261
msgid "Checks are always certain: a check in some possibilities only is rolled at once, even after castling or en passant."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/threecheck.js:265
msgid "A move that misses gives no check, even if the enemy king is attacked. Measuring never gives check."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/threecheck.js:269
msgid "A check left standing counts again after each of your moves, as long as the enemy king is still attacked."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/threecheck.js:274
msgid "The counters next to the player names show how many checks each side has given."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:363
msgid "Three 4 × 4 main levels, White's (W, lowest), Neutral (N) and Black's (B, highest), and four 2 × 2 attack boards at the back corners: QL1 and KL1 on the queen's and king's side of White, QL6 and KL6 of Black. The attack boards never move in this version."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:367
msgid "A square is named file, rank and board, such as b3N or z0QL1. Seen from above, all boards form one map with files z to e and ranks 0 to 9: b3W and b3N are the two levels of map square b3."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:371
msgid "Every move is an ordinary chess move on that map and may stop on any level of the target map square. Moving straight up or down is not a move."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:375
msgid "A piece on any level of a map square in between blocks the move. Gaps without a board are empty: pieces fly across them but cannot stop there."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:379
msgid "Pawns step forward (two map squares on their first move) and capture diagonally forward, onto any level. En passant lands on either level of the skipped square."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:383
msgid "A pawn promotes on the last rank of its file: rank 8 on files b and c, rank 9 on files z, a, d and e (for Black rank 1 and rank 0)."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:387
msgid "Castling from your second move on, if the king and that rook have not moved (in any possibility): on the king's side the king and the rook next to it swap places; on the queen's side, once the queen's square is empty, the king goes there and the corner rook to the king's square."
msgstr ""

#: src/variants/trid.js:391
msgid "Quantum tip: a ghost on either level of a map square blocks moves across it in its possibilities, and a piece split over both levels of one map square blocks it for certain. A ghost on the other level of your target square does not matter."
msgstr ""

